---
layout: base.njk
title: Full index
description: Every page on the site in one list — title, date, subjects and summary — to search with your browser's find in page.
---
{# The full index: the whole site as one flat list, for a reader who finds
   things with Ctrl+F. The search field in the bar needs scripting and is not
   shown without it; this is what that reader has instead. The footer links it
   from every page, and nav.njk puts a link in the search field's place
   whenever the field is not there.

   Written for find-in-page, which decides three things here:

   - Nothing is collapsed. Some browsers' find-in-page skips a closed
     <details>, and a clamped chip list hides what it clips, so every subject a
     post has is printed in full and tag_filter.njk is not included.
   - Nothing animates in. The site's entrance animations hold an element at
     opacity 0 through its delay, and a match inside one is a highlight on
     nothing.
   - Pages are large. Find-in-page searches only the page that is loaded, so
     `index_per_page` in site_settings.json defaults to 200 rows, against 40
     cards on the journal.

   The paging is in full_index.11tydata.js and in the fullIndex collection in
   eleventy_binary/lib/eleventy_config.js. #}
{% import "card.njk" as cards %}

{%- set total = collections.posts.length %}
{%- set paged = pagination.pages.length > 1 %}

<section class="shell" style="padding-block:clamp(3rem,9vh,5rem) 1rem;">
  <p class="eyebrow">{{ settings.name }}</p>
  <h1 class="display" style="margin-top:1rem;">{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    Every page on the site in one list, entries newest first. Search it with
    your browser's find in page: Ctrl+F, or Cmd+F on a Mac.
    {%- if paged %} The {{ total }} entries run to {{ pagination.pages.length }}
    pages, and find in page searches only the one you are on.{% endif %}
  </p>
  <hr class="rule-grad" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
</section>

{# The standing pages open page 1 only. Repeated on every page they would be
   the same few matches for every search, and the entries are what move. #}
{% if pagination.pageNumber == 0 and collections.sitePages.length %}
<section class="shell" style="padding-bottom:3rem;">
  <h2 class="display-md">Pages</h2>
  <div class="index-list" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    {% for item in collections.sitePages %}{{ cards.row(item) }}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="shell" style="padding-bottom:2rem;">
  <h2 class="display-md">Entries</h2>
  {% if indexPage.entries.length %}
  {% if paged %}
  <p class="micro" style="margin-top:0.75rem; color:var(--fg-muted);">
    {{ indexPage.first }}–{{ indexPage.first + indexPage.entries.length - 1 }} of {{ total }}
  </p>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="index-list" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    {% for post in indexPage.entries %}{{ cards.row(post) }}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="lede" style="padding-block:3rem;">Nothing published yet.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

{% include "pagination.njk" %}
